A||||6||batboy||swap meet adventures||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||05-08-2000||06:08 PM||||A couple buddies and I always rent vendor booths at the annual swap meet in Des Moines. I enlarged one of those PFF cards and posted it at my booth. This attracted 3 responses from people. One has been on the Forum before and remembers seeing my name. He has four Fieros, I believe.<P>Another guy gave me his exwife's phone number. Hmmm, that didn't sound good. His exwife bought a 85 GT and had it for 3 days before their 17 year old son ran it hot and blew a head gasket or cracked a head. He thought she might take a couple hundred for it. It has a wing and supposedly the body is in great condition. They live close to my parents, so next time I'm up to see my folks, I'll check out the Fiero too.<P>I chatted with a young guy who showed me his 86 Fiero SE. He's dreaming of a small block 350 and knew all about V8 Archie's. He cut a coil off each spring and had his car sitting pretty good. The neatest thing was that he used Fiat X-1/9 louvered intakes in place of the Fiero side intake. He had a matching one installed on the other side too. It looked damn good. Wish I had grabbed my camera. I passed the word of our Forum on to this guy too. Nice guy to talk to, like most Fiero owners.<P>I struck out looking for aluminum Batmobile heads for it's 350 motor. But, I did find a great 454 intake manifold and lots of misc. accessory brackets for my 72 Chevy truck motor I'm building. I'm telling you, people are mighty proud of their big block parts and charge a hefty price.<P>I managed to scope out some nice bargains. Lots of wheeling-dealing going on between vendors late on Sunday afternoon as we are packing up. I get my best deals then. We even had a powerglide tranny, truck fiberglass running boards, and a bunch of other junk given to us by other vendors that didn't want to pack it back home with them.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||frontal lobe||05-08-2000||10:58 PM||||Des Moines?  I wondered why you would hike all the way there for a swap meet.  Had to get out the old Rand McNally to check this out.  I guess if you are in eastern Kansas, that's not too far.  I've surmised from the fiero girl thread you are about 40 miles from Topeka?<P>Just curious.  What does it cost to rent a space a swap meet?||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-08-2000||11:35 PM||||At that swap meet, it's $20 per space. It's a way to sell old junk and buy new junk.||||reg||1
Z||000003||007DOUG||05-09-2000||12:14 AM||||Hey batboy,<P>Did you see any fiero parts at the swap meet. I mean anything fiero?<P>I was just at the Canfield OH swap this weekend, its huge. There wasn't a single fiero part. Nothing.<P>The same at Spring Carlisle. And Carlisle is fricking huge. I mean, no-on-site-parking-the-entire-grounds-are-filled, huge<P>I couldn't find a single wing, interior part, taillight, steering wheel. Not even a headlight motor or facia emblem.<P>The only item I've ever found to be close to a fiero is the ever-so-popular 14" aero wheel. The wheel found on practically every pontiac made.<P>What Gives? Why is the fiero (and its parts) treated like a plague?||||reg||13
Z||000004||batboy||05-09-2000||12:53 PM||||I found one Fiero steering wheel and asked how much for it, they said oh, so it's a Fiero steering wheel, we wondered what car it came off. I didn't take any Fiero parts, I'm hoarding them. When I have 3 Fieros, I'm bound to need those parts sooner or later.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||05-10-2000||04:05 AM||||I like those X-19 scoops,put some on an old Capri once,looked great,would actually be functional on a Fiero.Do you recall if they had one,or two scoops per side?<BR>Big block parts are pretty much in the same category as Alfa Romeo parts,maybe even more expensive it seems.Pretty darned nice though, just the same.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||05-10-2000||09:57 AM||||LowCG, he had one louver per side. It was about 4" X 10" or so (just guessing from memory) and looked really good. It blended in real nice, like it was designed for Fieros.||||reg||1
